# Docker build-context hygiene (change: desktop-smoke-ci).
#
# Every Dockerfile in this repo COPYs only pyproject.toml, uv.lock, README.md,
# src/, and docker/ — so everything else is pure build-context bloat. The local
# virtualenv alone is ~2 GB. This deny-list keeps the context to a few MB (fast
# to send to the daemon locally, and a small transfer on a CI runner). It is a
# deny-list, not an allow-list, so adding a new Dockerfile that needs another
# top-level path won't be silently starved of it — only these explicit paths
# are withheld.

# Python virtualenv + build/test caches (the dominant cost)
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# VCS, CI, editor, tooling metadata
.git/
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.kilo/

# Generated artifacts, results, logs, data not needed by any image build
artifacts/
node_modules/
tests/agenteval/results/
test_data/
*.log
STDOUT
dist/
results/
runs/
sys/

# Runtime / tooling output dirs (claude-flow, swarm, robotmcp artifacts) — none COPYed
.claude-flow/
.claude/
.swarm/
.robotmcp_artifacts/
.robotmcp_artifacts_e2e/

# Tests, docs, specs, experiments, scratch — no Dockerfile COPYs these
tests/
docs/
experiments/
openspec/
lab/

# Root-level markdown/scratch (keep README.md — the Dockerfiles COPY it)
*.md
!README.md
